#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:6
#: b62fd3fc9b624aaa89094e5b1bb2d2ae
msgid "Multiwii Serial Protocol (MSP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:8
#: 8ac92daca5f94f2fa12a4ea14474ac2b
msgid "ArduPilot supports the MSP protocol for telemetry and sensors via any of its serial ports. This allows ArduPilot to send its telemetry data to MSP compatible devices, such as DJI goggles, for On Screen Display (OSD) (See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2`). It can also be used by external OSDS, such as MWOSD, when setup for MSP protocol (ie betaflight/Inav), instead of MAVLink protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:11
#: b08067fc7ed545f6b48684860fb13922
msgid "Protocol overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:13
#: 0ae5be0f063044a1803b5a0995c0d107
msgid "MSP is the main communication protocol used by all Betaflight derived flight stacks. It's a binary message based protocol used for control, telemetry and sensors. ArduPilot's MSP protocol module is ported from Betaflight and iNav, and supports both MSPV1 and MSPV2. It also supports iNav's MSPV2 sensor messages for:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:17
#: 66e5e87f8574414ea76d597e6b1d1c1a
msgid "lidar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:18
#: 529a953ab2d34020bf589c064d33295e
msgid "optical flow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:19
#: 2ebbc77d6f264ffd8ec0b5d61d82f57e
msgid "gps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:20
#: b54eb5af7fda4565812c1e7cabc32e1d
msgid "barometer (future)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:21
#: f91bb2c415d248628d0a83b25a24c78d
msgid "magnetometer (future)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:22
#: c178fa5673324d44a03ec48668c33984
msgid "airspeed (future)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:24
#: ef9540bfb9f74fef885a33f8eebcff7f
msgid "At the moment, the ArduPilot implementation supports only telemetry and sensor messages. So currently ArduPilot works with DJI FPV goggles, but can't be controlled by the Betaflight configurator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:28
#: 15847c76b4e049468fe863fc356e4150
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:30
#: 2779a673a3574feb95b8fa8631a3dabb
msgid "MSP requires a free serial port, and its speed defaults to 115200 baud. Below SERIAL2 is used for the examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:32
#: b042680077554d04955a6fda1bbf8180
msgid "There are 3 MSP backends selected by serial protocol:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:34
#: 71270ba8c6bc471fba2c548dce70ee90
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 33 is for DJI FPV or RE Goggles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:35
#: 3b5c5c6f192d4c81add6a48d027de7b1
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 32 is for sensors or generic MSP telemetry usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:36
#: 20f6cf533394451abae84b57a1d067d2
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 42 is for DisplayPort for DJI goggle using wtf-os firmware, HDZero, Walksnail, or DisplayPort MWOSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:38
#: 7921dd8534054de1ac3a0c436a589a3f
msgid "There are 2 different DJI telemetry protocols to try to maintain compatibility with DJI's evolving hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:40
#: 10adaf54493e4de6a34688029ca65543
msgid "When :ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL<SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 33 is selected the protocol decoder can work in polling mode (default) or in \"telemetry push\" mode. When working in polling mode, both TX and RX must be connected to the MSP telemetry transceiver. While in push mode only the TX line is used. To enable push mode, simply set :ref:`MSP_OPTIONS<MSP_OPTIONS>` bit 0 to \"1\"; to disable set it to \"0\" (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-msp-overview.rst:42
#: 8e658d5c27284ad5993ec1cf30ceac42
msgid "MSP sensors such as the Matek 3901-L0X are supported by both protocols."
msgstr ""
